+# P1-A — concentration / aux-B program
+
+**Status:** open Level-3 gate under G1. This branch is reserved for the concentration proof program and must not absorb Level-2 renewal assumptions.
+
+## Target
+
+Assume the finite-obstruction reduction has supplied a closed recurrent nonproductive carrier. Prove that the expanding wedge contribution generated by recurrent behavior has nonzero projection inside that closed recurrent carrier.
+
+Equivalently, close the load-bearing implication currently denoted **concentration / aux-B**:
+
+```text
+closed recurrent carrier
+=> phi_dom != 0.
+```
+
+The current strongest downstream route is then
+
+```text
+phi_dom != 0
+=> Galois propagation of wedge nonvanishing
+=> full wedge span / span-rich carrier
+=> productivity.
+```
+
+## Independence rule
+
+This program may assume G1 when studying the finite carrier. It must **not** import G1b-2 renewal finiteness as a proof ingredient except through the already-stated premise that the finite carrier exists.
+
+Concentration and renewal finiteness are distinct gates.
+
+## Provenance requirement
+
+Before this branch can claim a closed theorem, import and audit the missing v16/later source for:
+
+- the exact definition of the dominant wedge functional;
+- the Galois-conjugacy/nonvanishing propagation theorem;
+- the precise span-rich-to-productivity implication used downstream;
+- the exact aux-B/concentration statement.
+
+Until then, executable work is diagnostic/certificate support and must say so.
+
+## Preferred executable surface
+
+New computation is Mojo-first.
+
+Priority diagnostics should operate on compact SCC/state IDs and exact integer/rational wedge data. Avoid rebuilding Python-shaped symbolic objects in hot loops.
+
+Useful finite experiments include:
+
+1. decompose recurrent wedge mass by SCC/carrier;
+2. identify which transient-to-recurrent transfers can erase the dominant component;
+3. produce exact certificates for a nonzero dominant projection when present;
+4. preserve any specimen where dominant contribution remains outside the target carrier as a countermodel to an overstrong concentration lemma.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+P1-A is closed only when all of the following hold:
+
+- concentration is stated without hidden FI, unimodularity, or extra boundary assumptions;
+- the proof starts from the exact finite closed-carrier hypotheses available under G1;
+- dominant nonvanishing in the carrier is derived, not sampled;
+- the imported Galois propagation source is audited against the same wedge representation/conventions used in the proof;
+- span-rich productivity is assembled with its exact hypotheses;
+- the machine/prose ledgers are updated without conflating this gate with G1b-2.
